'''trepanize''' (trep′an-īz), ''v. t.''; pret. and pp. ''trepanized'', ppr. ''trepanizing''. [< ''trepan''<sup>1</sup> + ''-ize''.] To trepan.

{{smaller block|Some have been cured . . . by ''trepanizing'' the scull, or drawing bones from it.
{{right|''Jer. Taylor'', Miseries of Temporal Life.}}}}
